  "note": "Correction: an abstract Γ-action not coming from Γ_k is not a descent datum at all (descent data relative to k'/k are Γ_k-actions, 20167), rather than a non-effective one. The phrasing may be the lecturer's (oral); the item was already marked uncertain.",
  "correction": {
   "old": "The action of $\\Gamma_k$ on $X'$ is determined by the action of the abstract group $\\Gamma$; so morphisms over $k'$ are compatible with descent data iff they commute with $\\Gamma$. An action of $\\Gamma$ need not come from $\\Gamma_k$: then the descent data are not effective.",
   "new": "The action of $\\Gamma_k$ on $X'$ is determined by the action of the abstract group $\\Gamma$; so morphisms over $k'$ are compatible with descent data iff they commute with $\\Gamma$. An action of $\\Gamma$ need not come from $\\Gamma_k$: it is then not a descent datum, and $X'$ need not descend."
  }
 },
